#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "52fc2fee-c015-55e0-b411-03c86d5992e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5447" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/10c3819b661a1831f747c949089a9133b4d0df7b07a66efe588c12bab469136e.png)\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/0cd1d198e714f41437302bdf21c17979409a533d3055b5b4dc519855d6fc8efb.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/e8a14ffbaab4597a2a4a7c9a6bad61dabbc4970fc22c3ed2eb28b2594a670938.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "8b7758b4-e0ec-5872-90d7-1136c9716574" :question/math-academy-id "e-6682" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/73f0065d4d4768a2c3432559702c2db28fefd050194a5bcdfe44ac3e0b736c82.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/fe82a0c8616e43c9d8db0b2892a145fcabf4cfa17bd3d4e033a1349cd25921ee.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb10166-6de0-58ae-9c5a-1768164fafe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333225} {:answer/id #uuid "183ad56d-58ec-5cde-90c9-3d1d3e3d2e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333226} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6d2dc2-589b-539f-ad79-4d4b1963b84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333227} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3436aa-bc6f-5420-90bf-14ca61e1eb69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333228} {:answer/id #uuid "c04776d6-80c4-5774-b0fe-c35c114e64a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183ad56d-58ec-5cde-90c9-3d1d3e3d2e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333226} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ae9de8-3f45-5dd4-9da7-b22a8a5e5c02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afcd3422-c3b2-56a7-a256-45fffe148caa" :question/math-academy-id "q-12033" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(3,3),$ and $(5,-2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(5,-2)$\n- $(-2,-5)$\n- $(3,12)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-5),(3,12),(5,13).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed6836d0-0024-58ed-863b-412e0c295626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,2)$ and $(-5,7)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333232} {:answer/id #uuid "43c5aaed-d5e6-5d0c-8c04-201104fbaa52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,-2)$ and $(5,-7)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333233} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a74d52-e29c-56e0-ab6a-bc1616c5e980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,2)$ and $(-5,7)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333234} {:answer/id #uuid "4c474c4e-cada-5c3a-9141-64c2d6f0708f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,-2)$ and $(-5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333235} {:answer/id #uuid "ef2cea96-ddb1-529a-a4bc-db2ff2cc83c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,2)$ and $(-5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6836d0-0024-58ed-863b-412e0c295626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,2)$ and $(-5,7)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333232} :answer-field/id #uuid "855f7050-5914-50a0-868a-e2bb3f0db43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9f71d03-299c-533e-bd5f-2dfe8453c281" :question/math-academy-id "q-159797" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(1,1)$ and $B(-1,2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(2,2)$ and ${B}^{′}(-5,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6f322ad-95a5-5c05-b401-86954c9727d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/02b7a778b46085876e5269e0b088dde52293d5230cd0312459ec21c8b2600f71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283468} {:answer/id #uuid "c784b9a