n-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042d6be9-8a88-5faa-9445-209423362a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "042d6be9-8a88-5faa-9445-209423362a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333239} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6df545-8b64-59e0-b787-0eff1694b197" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/bl